CommitDate: Wed Oct 28 17:55:20 2026 +0800

    [Refactor] Extract AscendStore lookup and layerwise modules (#19885)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Move AscendStore lookup client/server into `lookup_key.py`. Extract
    layerwise transfer threads and cache layout into the `layerwise`
    package, then move layerwise metadata types and helpers there. Update
    production imports, existing test imports, and mock targets to use the
    new module locations. The changes make lookup and layerwise ownership
    explicit without changing the transfer protocol or user configuration.
    Current main's serving-index endpoint isolation is retained in the
    extracted lookup helper.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This is an internal code organization refactor; no release note
    fragment is needed.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `bash format.sh ci`, changed Python syntax compilation, and `git diff
    --check` — passed.
    - Eight existing lookup client and endpoint tests passed through a
    temporary local bootstrap for unavailable vLLM dependencies. These
    include reset acknowledgement/rejection, lookup failure/cleanup, receive
    timeout setup, and real ZeroMQ IPC binds for independent dense DP
    replicas. Both CPU configurations and selected NPU execution passed in
    CI on this head.
    - `git rebase origin/main` — passed on the linear branch based directly
    on current main.
    - The production code and affected existing tests match the previously
    validated `e9acd1b9a` tree. Its [E2E
    workflow](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40561203390)
    passed both vLLM CPU configurations, selected 310P/A2/A3/A5 tests,
    upstream E2E, and `ci-gate` on attempt 2. The current-head CI result is
    recorded below.
    
    - CI on `f310064cd`: [E2E workflow 40606903613, attempt
    2](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40606903613)
    completed successfully. Both vLLM CPU configurations, all selected
    310P/A2/A3/A5 hardware test jobs, upstream E2E, pre-commit, and
    `ci-gate` passed. The first attempt encountered a 310P runtime/driver
    error during asynchronous H2D copy; the same commit passed on rerun
    without code or timeout changes. Optional cache-build and
    coverage-upload jobs were skipped by workflow conditions.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: Existing affected tests
    retained; focused lookup checks passed locally, selected integration
    coverage passed in CI on this head.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: No new behavior; reset test mock targets
    follow the extracted implementation.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: Focused lookup failure/cleanup
    and reset rejection checks passed; selected CI checks passed on this
    head.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: Existing tests retained;
    distinguish local dependency-bootstrap checks from CI hardware
    execution.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: No performance claim or benchmark is
    included.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    Signed-off-by: weijinqian0 <1184188277@qq.com>

